  ["The fridge stops humming mid-sentence.","Personification",["Simile","Rhyme"],"Makes the fridge sound like someone talking who has been cut off",["Makes the fridge sound broken forever","Describes a song"],"shows how the background noise of modern life suddenly stops",["shows the family is poor","shows the fridge is dangerous"]],
  ["a row of shut eyes","Metaphor",["Simile","Onomatopoeia"],"Makes the dead screens seem asleep",["Makes the screens seem scary","Shows the screens are new"],"suggests the devices that usually watch the family have closed",["shows the family is tired","shows the TV is broken"]],
  ["a dog asks the dark a question","Personification",["Alliteration","Hyperbole"],"The barking sounds puzzled, like a question",["The dog is angry","The dog is asleep"],"adds to the strange, quiet mood of the blackout",["shows the dog is lost","shows the street is dangerous"]],
  ["the drawer of everything","Metaphor (a funny name for a junk drawer)",["Simile","Onomatopoeia"],"Creates humour and a sense of an ordinary family home",["Shows the family is messy and careless","Describes a shop"],"makes the family feel real and familiar",["shows they own too much","shows Dad is angry"]],
  ["My brother stops scrolling. My sister stops sulking.","Parallel sentences and alliteration",["Simile","Rhetorical question"],"The matching pattern shows everyone changing at once",["Makes it sound like a list of chores","Slows the poem to a stop"],"shows the family coming back to each other",["shows the children are in trouble","shows they are bored"]],
  ["We laugh at nothing. We laugh at everything.","Repetition and contrast (paradox)",["Onomatopoeia","Simile"],"Captures the giddy, happy feeling",["Shows they are confused","Shows they are mocking someone"],"shows the joy of being together without screens",["shows they are scared of the dark","shows nothing happened"]],
  ["loud as a shout","Simile",["Metaphor","Personification"],"Makes the lights feel harsh and sudden",["Makes the lights feel gentle","Describes a song"],"shows the normal world crashing back in",["shows the power company is angry","shows someone is yelling"]],
  ["wants to be the first to blow the candles out","Symbolism",["Onomatopoeia","Hyperbole"],"The candles stand for the closeness the family found",["The candles are a fire risk","It is a birthday"],"shows the family wants to hold on to the moment",["shows they are afraid of the dark","shows the candles are expensive"]]
